      <div class="flex-1">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-light text-charcoal mb-2">Carver's Pattern Maker</h2>
        <p class="font-ui text-[11px] tracking-widest uppercase text-charcoal/40 mb-4">Wood carving</p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/70 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Turn a photograph of a spoon, a bowl, or any carvable object into a pattern you can print at true scale. Tap the object and the shape is traced for you. Set the length — any size you like, from a teaspoon to an oar — then add a centerline, a grid, and layout lines to strike against. Photograph a top view and a side view and both print together with shared registration marks, so they line up when you transfer them to the blank.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/60 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Everything happens on your device — your photographs are never uploaded. Free to use, and the printed page is always true to the size you asked for.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
          <a href="{{ '/pattern_maker/' | url }}"
             class="inline-block font-ui text-xs tracking-widest uppercase border border-charcoal text-charcoal px-8 py-3 hover:bg-charcoal hover:text-ground transition-colors text-center"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Open Pattern Maker →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# Tool card: Bowl Designer #}
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-12 items-start">
